Copyright (C) 2026 Gopex LLC. All rights reserved.

Entity definitions for idTech3Radiant editor.
Defines new entity types for engine features:
  - Director zones and spawn points
  - DMM destructible objects
  - Projected lights (flashlights)
  - Cloth simulation
  - HDR skybox configuration
  - Background map cameras
  - Choreography marks
  - Response rule triggers
===========================================================================
*/

/*QUAKED info_director_zone (0.5 0.0 1.0) (-8 -8 -8) (8 8 8)
AI Director threat zone.
Places a pacing zone that affects spawn budgets and intensity.
--------- KEYS ---------
targetname : zone name for Lua reference
threat : threat level (0=none, 1=low, 2=medium, 3=high, 4=extreme)
budget_mult : spawn budget multiplier (default 1.0)
--------- NOTES ---------
Draw the zone bounds using the brush-defined AABB.
The Director uses these zones to adjust spawn frequency.
*/

/*QUAKED info_director_spawn (1.0 0.5 0.0) (-16 -16 -24) (16 16 32)
AI Director spawn point.
Enemies spawn here when the Director triggers a wave.
--------- KEYS ---------
spawn_type : Director spawn type name (e.g. "zombie", "runner")
min_intensity : minimum Director intensity to activate (0.0-1.0)
max_intensity : maximum Director intensity to activate (0.0-1.0)
--------- NOTES ---------
Place multiple spawn points throughout the map.
The Director selects spawn points based on player proximity and intensity.
*/

/*QUAKED func_destructible (0.8 0.4 0.0) ?
DMM destructible object.
A brush entity that can be damaged, deformed, and fractured.
--------- KEYS ---------
dmm_material : material type (0=wood, 1=glass, 2=thin_metal, 3=thick_metal, 4=concrete, 5=stone, 6=ice, 7=plastic)
dmm_health : hit points before fracture (default 100)
dmm_fracture_mode : fracture pattern (0=voronoi, 2=splinter, 3=shatter, 5=crumble, 6=tear)
dmm_min_fragments : min fragment count (default 4)
dmm_max_fragments : max fragment count (default 12)
dmm_break_sound : sound shader on destruction
dmm_stress_sound : sound shader on damage
--------- NOTES ---------
Common presets:
  Wood door: material=0, health=150, fracture=2 (splinter)
  Glass pane: material=1, health=20, fracture=3 (shatter)
  Concrete wall: material=4, health=500, fracture=5 (crumble)
*/

/*QUAKED light_projected (0.8 0.8 0.2) (-8 -8 -8) (8 8 8) SHADOWS VOLUMETRIC
Projected spotlight / flashlight.
A spotlight with optional shadow casting and volumetric cone.
--------- KEYS ---------
_color : light color (RGB, default 1 1 1)
light : intensity (default 300)
cone_angle : spotlight cone angle in degrees (default 45)
range : light range (default 512)
cookie : projected texture shader (optional)
volumetric_density : fog density inside cone (default 0.1)
--------- SPAWNFLAGS ---------
SHADOWS : enable shadow casting
VOLUMETRIC : enable volumetric cone rendering
*/

/*QUAKED func_cloth (0.4 0.8 0.4) ?
Cloth simulation surface.
A brush entity that simulates cloth physics at runtime.
--------- KEYS ---------
width : grid width in particles (default 16)
height : grid height in particles (default 16)
spacing : distance between particles (default 4)
pin_edge : pinned edge (0=top, 1=bottom, 2=left, 3=right)
wind_strength : wind force (default 0)
wind_dir : wind direction vector
material : cloth material shader
--------- NOTES ---------
The brush defines the cloth's initial flat shape.
Pin one edge for hanging cloth (flags, banners, curtains).
Pin two corners for stretched cloth (tarps, canopies).
*/

/*QUAKED info_bgmap_camera (0.0 0.5 1.0) (-8 -8 -8) (8 8 8)
Background map camera point.
Defines a camera position for menu background map flythroughs.
--------- KEYS ---------
fov : field of view (default 90)
time : time in cycle at this point (seconds)
target : targetname of next camera point
--------- NOTES ---------
Chain camera points using target/targetname.
The engine interpolates smoothly between points.
*/

/*QUAKED info_choreo_mark (0.5 0.0 0.5) (-4 -4 -4) (4 4 4)
Choreography position mark.
Marks a position used by scripted scene sequences.
--------- KEYS ---------
targetname : reference name for scene scripts
scene : scene name this mark belongs to
actor : actor name positioned here
*/

/*QUAKED trigger_response (0.5 0.5 0.0) ?
Response rule trigger volume.
When a player enters this brush, triggers a dialogue response concept.
--------- KEYS ---------
concept : response concept to evaluate (e.g. "entered_danger_zone")
zone : zone name for response context
--------- NOTES ---------
Use with the Response Rules system (g_response.h).
The concept is evaluated against all registered rules.
*/

/*QUAKED info_navmesh_config (0.0 1.0 0.5) (-8 -8 -8) (8 8 8)
Navigation mesh configuration entity.
One per map. Overrides default Recast navmesh generation parameters.
--------- KEYS ---------
cell_size : rasterization cell size (default 0.3)
cell_height : rasterization cell height (default 0.2)
agent_height : agent height (default 2.0)
agent_radius : agent radius (default 0.6)
agent_max_climb : max step height (default 0.9)
agent_max_slope : max walkable slope degrees (default 45)
*/
